## What this company will tell you that others may not

- A sewer quote given without a camera inspection is a guess. Every job starts with video.
- Lining cannot fix a pipe that has lost its slope, sagged into a belly, or collapsed. Those
  lines need pipe bursting or conventional replacement.
- Colorado's expansive clay soils move pipe over time; bellies and offsets caused by that
  movement are a common reason a line needs bursting or a dig instead of a liner.
- Around Denver, the property owner usually owns the sewer lateral out to the main, often
  including the connection, but the rule depends on the city or special sanitation district.

